.\" tifea.1 - Man page for TIFEA (TAR Installer For Electron Applications)
.TH TIFEA 1 "August 2026" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tifea \- Atomic transactional installer for desktop Electron tarballs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tifea
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TIFEA
(TAR Installer For Electron Applications) is an atomic, self-healing, transactional command-line installer designed for prebuilt Linux desktop software packaged as tarballs (.tar.gz, .tar.xz).
.PP
TIFEA inspects archives without extracting them, builds deterministic installation plans, executes atomic actions backed by LIFO rollback state, generates Freedesktop-compliant .desktop entries, configures AppArmor/SELinux confinement, extracts bundled application icons (including embedded ASAR resources), and registers xdg-mime URL handlers.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinstall\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR [\fI--dry-run\fR] [\fI--yes\fR] [\fI--sandbox STRATEGY\fR]
Inspects \fIARCHIVE\fR and installs it into system directories (\fI/opt/<appid>\fR). Performs sandbox configuration, icon extraction, desktop entry creation, and SELinux relabeling.
.TP
\fBreinstall\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR [\fI--dry-run\fR] [\fI--yes\fR] [\fI--sandbox STRATEGY\fR]
Replaces an existing installation matching the application ID in \fIARCHIVE\fR while keeping the installation ledger updated.
.TP
\fBcheck\fR \fISYSTEM_PATH\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR
Compares an existing installation directory against an archive. Checks executable symlinks, desktop entries, icon hash integrity, xdg-open handlers, and SELinux path states without mutating system files.
.TP
\fBfix\fR \fISYSTEM_PATH\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR [\fI--yes\fR]
Runs check comparisons and repairs detected fixable discrepancies (such as broken symlinks or missing desktop entries). Prompts for baseline manifest adoption if none exists.
.TP
\fBlist\fR
Displays all installed applications managed by TIFEA.
.TP
\fBuninstall\fR \fIAPPID\fR
Safely removes the application matching \fIAPPID\fR, cleans up menu launchers and icon assets, and restores backups recorded in the installation manifest.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Preview the generated action plan and target directories without modifying the system.
.TP
.BR \-\-yes
Skip interactive prompts and accept plan confirmations automatically.
.TP
.BR \-\-sandbox \ \fISTRATEGY\fR
Select Electron sandbox strategy: \fBapparmor\fR, \fBsetuid\fR, or \fBno\-sandbox\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tifea/<appid>/manifest.json
Atomic transactional installation ledger storing step status and rollback metadata.
